"site-links examples" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Site links
		<header>Site links are the page shown's own links, for an app menu's end:  the real page it stands for (its `live` link, Fomantic UI's original for Spell UI's pages), and a way to report a problem with it.</>
	</>

	<section label="Types">
		<section label="The page's links" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "The page's links" description="The page shown is Button's API page:  its original is its family's, Fomantic's Button page, and the report link names the family.">
				<site-links current="#api" report="https://github.com/spell-app/spell-ui/issues/new?title={title}" pages="\[{ \"title\": \"Button\", \"href\": \"#usage\", \"live\": \"https://fomantic-ui.com/elements/button.html\", \"pages\": \[{ \"title\": \"API\", \"href\": \"#api\" }] }]" />
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="States">
		<section label="Nothing to link" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Nothing to link" description="A page with no original, and no `report`:  nothing is drawn and it takes no room, `:state(empty)`.">
				<site-links current="#home" pages="\[{ \"title\": \"Home\", \"href\": \"#home\" }]" />
			</example>
		</>
	</>
